  "raw_text": "The backup script desktop_backup was extended from covering only ~/Desktop to covering the full Linux home directory structure. On this system, $HOME is the functional equivalent of the Windows Desktop \u2014 the user works entirely in CLI and never looks at a graphical desktop, a discipline traced back to DEC VAX days. The same logical directory structure (info, picts, docs, etc.) that existed under \\Home\\John\\Desktop on Windows is reproduced directly under $HOME on Linux, so the script needed only to change its SRC variable from $HOME/Desktop to $HOME and adjust the dir list to reflect what actually exists in the Linux home.",
